[[Image:Gui_silent.png|right|Silenced indicator]]
{{feat
|type=metamagic
|prereq=ability to cast 1st-level spells
|reqfor=[[automatic silent spell]]
|desc=Silent [[spell]]s are cast without a verbal [[component]].
|use=A silenced spell occupies a [[spell slot]] one level higher than normal.
|bonus1=wizard
}}

==Notes==
* Most spells can be cast silenced, even those that normally do not have a verbal component. The only spells that cannot be silenced (in addition to all level 9 spells, which cannot be silenced due to the lack of spell slots above level 9) are the following. There is no correspondence between a spell's components and being on this list.
**[[Clarity]]
**[[Knock]]
**[[Scare]]

==Builder notes==
'''Item feat:''' No, but it can be added with custom content.

== Custom content notes ==
'''Removable:''' yes

'''Reusable:''' yes

'''Script:''' hardcoded

*This feat can be added to [[iprp_feats.2da]] and works as an item feat, but [[wizard]]s and [[divine]] spellcasters will only need to have the item equipped while preparing their [[spellbook]]s, not while [[rest]]ing or casting. [[Spellhook]]ing can be used to verify that the caster has the [[feat]] if it is used as an item feat.